@page "/terms"
@* PRD R16: reachable from every page. Draft outline from the prototype, not reviewed legal text (D10, gate G13). *@

<SeoHead Title="Terms of use · Tax Buddy" Description="The terms for using Tax Buddy. Draft pending legal review." CanonicalPath="/terms" />

<PhoneBar Title="Terms of use" Back="/" />

@* Laid out as the prototype's infoPage in a narrow panel (F02 BD10). *@
<div class="narrow">
<article class="panel prose" aria-labelledby="page-title">
    <h1 id="page-title" tabindex="-1">Terms of use</h1>
    <DraftLegalNotice />

    <section class="section"><h3>Using Tax Buddy</h3><p>Browsing is free and needs no account. You sign in with your Google account to message accountants, review them or publish a profile. Signing in with Microsoft is planned.</p></section>

    <section class="section"><h3>Your account</h3><p>When you first sign in you choose to be a client or an accountant. An account is one or the other. You agree to these terms and the privacy policy when you create your account.</p></section>

    <section class="section"><h3>Accountant profiles</h3><p>Accountants write their own profiles and are responsible for what they say. Tax Buddy doesn't check licences or qualifications.</p></section>

    <section class="section"><h3>Reviews</h3><p>A client can review an accountant who has replied to them, once, and can change or delete it. Reviews must describe the reviewer's own experience.</p></section>

    <section class="section"><h3>Reports and blocking</h3><p>Anyone signed in can report a profile, review or conversation, and block someone from messaging them. Tax Buddy may remove content or close accounts that break these terms.</p></section>

    <section class="section"><h3>Agreements between you</h3><p>Work, fees and deadlines are agreed between the client and the accountant. Tax Buddy is not a party to them.</p></section>

    <p class="muted small mt-4">Version @TaxBuddy.Web.Domain.LegalText.CurrentVersion.</p>
</article>
</div>
